{"id": "section-body-26999", "title": "Benzodiazepine withdrawal", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-three", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MENTAL HEALTH CONDITIONS", "Substance Related Disorder", "Benzodiazepine withdrawal"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-26999", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Benzodiazepine withdrawal", "runs": [{"text": "Benzodiazepine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "withdrawal"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27000", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Benzodiazepine addiction may occur after only a few weeks of use. Withdrawal symptoms on abrupt dose reduction or cessation includes anxiety, nervousness, irritability, depersonalization, delirium and seizures, increased sweating, sound sensitivity, nausea, difficulty concentrating, myoclonus, tremor, weakness and fatigue. Gradual tapering of the benzodiazepine is recommended to facilitate discontinuation.", "runs": [{"text": "Benzodiazepine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "addiction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occur"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "only"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "few"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weeks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "use."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Withdrawal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "abrupt"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reduction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cessation includes anxiety, nervousness, irritability, depersonalization, delirium and seizures, increased sweating, sound sensitivity, nausea, difficulty concentrating, myoclonus, tremor, weakness and fatigue. Gradual tapering of the benzodiazepine is recommended to facilitate discontinuation."}]}, {"id": "body-27002", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-27003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "The therapeutic relationship between client and doctor is extremely important in initiating dose reduction.", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapeutic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "relationship"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "between"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "client"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "doctor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "extremely"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "important"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "initiating"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reduction."}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27004", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Confirm benzodiazepine dependence – ascertain usage, history of previous withdrawal symptoms; a urine screen may be necessary", "runs": [{"text": "Confirm"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "benzodiazepine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dependence"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "–"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ascertain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usage,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "previous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "withdrawal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "urine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "screen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may be necessary"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27005", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Establish full dosage of all benzodiazepines being taken, including those prescribed by other medical practitioners", "runs": [{"text": "Establish"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "full"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dosage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "all"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "benzodiazepines"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "being"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "taken,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "including"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "those"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "prescribed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "other"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "practitioners"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27006", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Take time to explain negative impact of ongoing benzodiazepine use, benefits of stopping, and concepts like tolerance and withdrawal", "runs": [{"text": "Take"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "time"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "explain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "negative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "impact"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ongoing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "benzodiazepine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "use,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "benefits"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stopping,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "concepts"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "like"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tolerance and withdrawal"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27007", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Encourage the patient not to seek medication from other doctors.", "runs": [{"text": "Encourage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seek"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medication"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "other"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "doctors."}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27008", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Evaluate and optimize management of comorbid substance use disorders, mental illness, and general health conditions.", "runs": [{"text": "Evaluate and optimize"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "management of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "comorbid substance"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "use disorders, mental"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "illness, and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "general health conditions."}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27009", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Avoid abrupt withdrawal of benzodiazepines; be prepared to take time. Negotiate each reduction with the patient. Individualize regular monitoring and motivation.", "runs": [{"text": "Avoid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "abrupt"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "withdrawal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "benzodiazepines;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "prepared"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "take"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "time."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Negotiate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "each"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reduction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient. Individualize regular monitoring and motivation."}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27010", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Long-term follow-up with repeated motivation may be necessary to prevent relapse.", "runs": [{"text": "Long-term"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "follow-up"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "repeated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "motivation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "necessary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "prevent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "relapse."}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27012", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Replace short-acting benzodiazepine with an equivalent diazepam (long-acting benzodiazepine) dose equivalent doses to diazepam 5 mg are:", "runs": [{"text": "Replace short-acting benzodiazepine with an equivalent diazepam (long-acting benzodiazepine) dose equivalent doses to diazepam 5 mg are:"}]}, {"id": "body-27013", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "D: clonazepam (PO) 0.25–1 mg 24hourly", "runs": [{"text": "D:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "clonazepam"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "0.25–1"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}]}, {"id": "body-27014", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-27015", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: lorazepam (PO) 0.5 mg 24hourly", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "lorazepam"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "0.5"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}]}, {"id": "body-27016", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Higher doses may be required for patients who are dependent on both alcohol and benzodiazepines. Inpatient assessment and initiation of benzodiazepine tapering may be warranted in these patients.", "runs": [{"text": "Higher"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "doses"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "required"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "who"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dependent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "both"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "alcohol"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "benzodiazepines."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Inpatient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "assessment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and initiation of benzodiazepine tapering may be warranted in these patients."}]}, {"id": "body-27018", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Reduction is done according to clinical response.", "runs": [{"text": "Reduction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "done"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "according"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "response."}]}, {"id": "body-27019", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: diazepam (PO).", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "diazepam"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)."}]}, {"id": "body-27020", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Reduce daily dose every 1–2 weeks by 10 mg/day until a daily dose of 50 mg. Then reduce every 1–2 weeks by 5 mg/day until a daily dose of 30 mg. Then reduce every 1–2 weeks by 2.5 mg/day until a daily dose of 20 mg. Then reduce every 1–2 weeks by 1.25 mg/day until stopped.", "runs": [{"text": "Reduce"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "every"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1–2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weeks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "10"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg/day"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "until"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "50"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Then"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reduce"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "every"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1–2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weeks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg/day"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "until a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "30"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Then"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reduce"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "every"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1–2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weeks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2.5"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg/day"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "until"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "20"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Then"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reduce"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "every"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1–2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weeks by 1.25 mg/day until stopped."}]}, {"id": "body-27021", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "If symptoms reappear, increase the dose a little and reduce dose over longer intervals. No more than one week’s duration of therapy is generally issued at one time.", "runs": [{"text": "If symptoms reappear, increase the dose a little and reduce dose over longer intervals. No more than one week’s duration of therapy is generally issued at one time."}]}, {"id": "body-27023", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Opioid overdose", "runs": [{"text": "Opioid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "overdose"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-27024-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Note: Initial doses of Naloxone above 2 mg can induce severe withdrawal, with the risk of vomiting and aspiration; very high doses above 10 mg may even be life threatening", "runs": [{"text": "Note: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Initial doses of Naloxone above 2 mg can induce severe withdrawal, with the risk of vomiting and aspiration; very high doses above 10 mg may even be life threatening"}]}, {"id": "body-27026", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Overdose Don’ts", "runs": [{"text": "Overdose", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Don’ts", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-27027", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Do not leave the person alone by him/herself as they could stop breathing", "runs": [{"text": "Do"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leave"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "person"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "alone"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "him/herself"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "they"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "could"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stop"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "breathing"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27028", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Do not induce vomiting or feed orally as the client may aspirate", "runs": [{"text": "Do"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "induce"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vomiting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "feed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "orally"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "client"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aspirate"}], "list": {"level": 4, "numberingId": "349"}}, {"id": "body-27029", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Admit for continued observation for a minimum of 4 hours after administration of Naloxone. The client should be advised to avoid using any opioids or other drugs that may cause CNS depression for at least 24 hours and to ensure they do not stay alone during that period.", "runs": [{"text": "Admit for continued observation for a minimum of 4 hours after administration of Naloxone. The client should be advised to avoid using any opioids or other drugs that may cause CNS depression for at least 24 hours and to ensure they do not stay alone during that period."}]}, {"id": "body-27031", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Psychiatric Disorders Associated with Epilepsy", "runs": [{"text": "Psychiatric"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Disorders"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Epilepsy"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "359"}}, {"id": "body-27032", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Epilepsy is a disorder of the brain characterized by an enduring predisposition to generate epileptic seizures and by the biologic, cognitive, psychological, and social consequences of this condition. This association may reflect the anatomical and neurobiological source of both epileptic seizures and the behavioral manifestations. Antiepileptic drugs (AEDs) can play a role in the genesis of psychiatric symptoms; on the other hand, some psychotropic medications can lower the seizure threshold and provoke epileptic seizures.", "runs": [{"text": "Epilepsy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disorder"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "brain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characterized"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "enduring"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "predisposition"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "generate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "epileptic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seizures"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "biologic, cognitive, psychological, and social consequences of this condition. This association may reflect the anatomical and neurobiological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "source"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "both"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "epileptic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seizures"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "behavioral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "manifestations."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Antiepileptic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "drugs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(AEDs)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "play"}, {"text": " "}, {"tex